WHAT "NON-COMMERCIAL" MEANS HERE

Teaching, learning, research, and use inside a school, college or
university are all welcome, including where that institution charges
tuition. Selling this material, putting it behind a paywall, or using it
in paid training or consulting is not. If your situation sits somewhere
between the two, write and ask — the answer is usually yes.

WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES NOT COVER

  Third-party material. The labs use public datasets from sources such
  as NYC Open Data, the US Census Bureau (TIGER), and NCES. The readings
  are other people's books and documentation. Screenshots show Esri's
  ArcGIS Pro. None of that is mine to license; each carries its own
  terms, and the original source is named wherever it is used.

  The site's code. The stylesheets, build hooks and demo scripts are
  software rather than course content, and are licensed under the MIT
  License (below).

  The gated lab material. The project instructions and reference answers
  are live assessment material and are not published openly. They are
  shared with instructors on request and are not covered by the open
  licence above.

